## Project Structure Guide

- `app/`: Next.js App Router **pages only** — `app/(home)/` (the `/` route and its
  loading state), `app/dashboard/page.tsx` plus nested `app/dashboard/statistics/`
  and `app/dashboard/generator/`, the results archive (`resultados/`,
  `resultados/[ano]/`, `concurso/[numero]/`, `numeros/`, `numeros/[numero]/`,
  `mega-da-virada/`),
  `about/`, `privacy/`, `terms/`, `sitemap.xml/`, `robots.ts`, `llms.txt/`,
  `indexnow-key.txt/`. Archive
  helpers live in `app/_lib/` and `app/_components/`. There is no `app/api/`.
  Never add a `loading.tsx` above archive routes (it turns 404s into soft 404s);
  links into archive routes must not prefetch (see AGENTS.md "SEO/pSEO invariants").
- `lib/api/handler.ts`: shared API contract; `server.ts` is its local/VPS Bun adapter (port 3201).
- `cloudflare/worker.ts`: staging vinext frontend Worker with API calls through
  private `DATA` binding to `MegaSenaData` SQLite in `cloudflare/data-object.ts`.
  `cloudflare/ingestion.ts` owns CAIXA refresh; `vite.config.ts` selects Worker
  database/transport adapters. `cloudflare.config.ts` owns bindings and Cron.
  On Bun, `next.config.js` forwards `/api/:path*` to `server.ts`. New endpoints
  belong in `lib/api/handler.ts`.
- `proxy.ts`: the Next.js 16 middleware (Next renamed `middleware` → `proxy`); mints
  the per-request CSP nonce and sets page security headers.
- `components/`: reusable UI using Tailwind semantic tokens and shadcn variants.
- `lib/`:
  - `lib/analytics/`: statistics engines and `bet-generator.ts`
  - `lib/api/`: CAIXA API client and response cache
  - `lib/security/`: CSP, HTTP guards, IP pseudonymization
  - `lib/db.ts`: `bun:sqlite` layer; `lib/constants.ts`: shared config (incl. `BASE_URL`)
- `db/`: SQLite database plus `db/migrations/*.sql`.
- `scripts/`: Bun CLIs such as `scripts/pull-draws.ts` for ingest/seeding.
- `tests/`: Vitest (`tests/lib`, `tests/components`, `tests/scripts`) and Playwright
  (`tests/app`).
- `docs/`: DEPLOY, SECURITY, PRIVACY, LGPD-COMPLIANCE, TERMS, INCIDENT-RESPONSE.
  Update `docs/PRIVACY.md` and `docs/LGPD-COMPLIANCE.md` whenever data collection,
  retention, or purpose changes.

Constraints:

- Read `AGENTS.md` first; it is the canonical agent contract for this repo.
- Keep changes minimal and targeted to explicitly requested areas.
- Place new Cursor rules under `.cursor/rules` with the `.mdc` extension.
- User-facing copy is pt-BR.
